<title>USA: HFS Inc closes $1 bln credit facility.</title>
<headline>HFS Inc closes $1 bln credit facility.</headline>
<dateline>PARSIPPANY, N.J. 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>HFS Inc said Thursday it has closed on $1 billion in syndicated credit facilities. The company said it would use the facilities for acquisitions and other generate corporate purposes.</p>
<p>The hotel frachisor and real estate brokerage firm said the transaction increased its credit facilities from $300 million.</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan Bank will serve as administrative agent. Chase Securities Inc served as arranger and advisor, HFS said.</p>
